<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #ffffff; --surface: #f7f8fa; --chrome: #eceef1; --border: #d5d9df; --text: #16191d; --muted: #545c66;
    --accent: #c2410c; --on-accent: #ffffff; --accent-subtle: #ffedd5; --on-accent-subtle: #9a3412; --teal: #0f766e;
    --shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(0,0,0,.14); --radius: 14px; color-scheme: light;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --bg: #1e2126; --surface: #25292f; --chrome: #2d3238; --border: #3c424a; --text: #e8eaed; --muted: #a8b0ba;
      --accent: #fb923c; --on-accent: #1c0d02; --accent-subtle: #431d0a; --on-accent-subtle: #fed7aa; --teal: #2dd4bf; color-scheme: dark;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; font: 400 17px/1.6 system-ui, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; color: var(--text); background: var(--bg); }
  a { color: inherit; }
  .wrap { max-width: 1120px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px; }
  header.top { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: 18px 0; }
  .brand { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; font-weight: 700; font-size: 22px; text-decoration: none; }
  .brand svg { flex: none; }
  .btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 12px 22px; border-radius: 10px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border: 2px solid transparent; }
  .btn.primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
  .btn.primary:hover { filter: brightness(1.08); }
  .btn.ghost { border-color: var(--border); }
  .btn.ghost:hover { background: var(--chrome); }
  .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--teal); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; padding: 32px 0 56px; }
  .eyebrow { display: inline-block; background: var(--accent-subtle); color: var(--on-accent-subtle); padding: 4px 12px; border-radius: 999px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(38px, 6vw, 64px); line-height: 1.05; margin: 14px 0 16px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .lead { font-size: 19px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 640px; margin: 0 0 26px; }
  .ctas { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; align-items: center; }
  .note { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 12px; }
  .shot { border-radius: var(--radius); overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow); border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--chrome); }
  .shot img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  section { padding: 56px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 4vw, 38px); line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 28px; max-width: 680px; }
  .grid { display: grid; gap: 18px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); }
  .card { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 22px; }
  .card h3 { margin: 10px 0 6px; font-size: 19px; }
  .card p { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 16px; }
  .icon { width: 40px; height: 40px; border-radius: 10px; background: var(--accent-subtle); color: var(--on-accent-subtle); display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .icon svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .steps { counter-reset: step; }
  .steps .card h3::before { counter-increment: step; content: counter(step); display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 30px; height: 30px; margin-right: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); font-size: 15px; }
  .problem .card { border-left: 4px solid var(--accent); }
  .price { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 18px; align-items: center; }
  .price .big { font-size: 64px; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; }
  .price ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  .also { font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
  details { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 14px 18px; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  summary { font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; }
  details p { color: var(--muted); margin: 10px 0 2px; }
  .final { text-align: center; }
  .final .ctas { justify-content: center; }
  footer { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 28px 0 40px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); text-align: center; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hero { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.25fr; align-items: center; padding: 48px 0 72px; }
    .price { grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="top">
    <a class="brand" href="#top" aria-label="Kerfline home">
      <svg width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true"><rect width="32" height="32" rx="7" fill="var(--accent)"/><path d="M8 23C11 9 21 9 24 23" fill="none" stroke="var(--on-accent)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="24" cy="23" r="3" fill="var(--on-accent)"/></svg>
      Kerfline
    </a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="https://kerfline.surge.sh">Open Kerfline</a>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <div class="hero">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Free · No account · Works offline</span>
        <h1>Draw it. Cut it. Free.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Kerfline is a free vector editor for makers and students. Design for laser cutters, vinyl and print, right in your browser.</p>
        <div class="ctas">
          <a class="btn primary" href="https://kerfline.surge.sh">Open Kerfline</a>
          <a class="btn ghost" href="kerfline.html" download>Download for offline use</a>
        </div>
        <p class="note">Nothing to install. Your drawings stay on your computer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="shot"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="The Kerfline editor: a tool column on the left, a poster with a sun and stars on the page, colour swatches and the Objects panel on the right" width="1440" height="900"></div>
    </div>

    <section class="problem" aria-labelledby="problem">
      <h2 id="problem">Drawing software shouldn't cost you twice</h2>
      <p class="sub">Two things people complain about most in professional drawing software:</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card"><h3>Paying again and again</h3><p>Pro tools cost hundreds a year, and older versions stop being supported, so you are pushed to upgrade even when yours still works.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Losing your work</h3><p>Big files crash, and the work disappears with them.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how">
      <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
      <p class="sub">From idea to machine in three steps.</p>
      <div class="grid steps">
        <div class="card"><h3>Open it</h3><p>Any modern browser, or the offline file. No install, no sign-up.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Draw</h3><p>Shapes, curves, text in built-in fonts, layers, Weld and Trim, rulers and snapping.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Make it</h3><p>DXF for the laser or CNC, SVG for vinyl and the web, PDF or PNG for print.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="features">
      <h2 id="features">Made for making</h2>
      <p class="sub">Everything is included. There is no "pro" version.</p>
      <div class="grid">
        <div class="card"><div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 20L20 4"/><circle cx="20" cy="4" r="2"/></svg></div><h3>Maker styles</h3><p>One click for laser cut (red hairline), score (blue), engrave (black fill) or vinyl cut.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14 3H6v18h12V7z"/><path d="M14 3v4h4M8 13h8M8 17h5"/></svg></div><h3>DXF export</h3><p>Millimetres, smooth curves to 0.05 mm, and colours that laser software understands.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5 3h11l3 3v15H5z"/><path d="M8 3v5h7V3M8 21v-7h8v7"/></svg></div><h3>Never lose work</h3><p>Saves after every change, offers to restore after a crash, and can keep a copy in a folder on your own drive.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 7v5l3 3"/></svg></div><h3>Files never expire</h3><p>Every version opens every older file. The format is open and documented. SVG and PDF export stay free.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 18C6 6 18 18 20 6"/><rect x="2.5" y="16.5" width="3" height="3"/><rect x="18.5" y="4.5" width="3" height="3"/></svg></div><h3>Real vector tools</h3><p>Pen and Bézier tools, node editing, text to curves, gradients, pages, guides and snapping.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><div class="icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="12" rx="2"/><path d="M8 20h8M12 16v4"/></svg></div><h3>Runs anywhere</h3><p>Windows, Mac, Linux, Chromebooks and school computers. One file, no install.</p></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="price">
      <div class="price">
        <div>
          <h2 id="price">Price</h2>
          <div class="big">Free</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <ul>
            <li>One version with everything in it</li>
            <li>No account, no ads, no tracking</li>
            <li>No editions or add-ons to buy, ever</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="also">Made by SRIVELTECH to help STEM and 3D-printing learners. SRIVELTECH does not earn from Kerfline.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="faq">
      <h2 id="faq">Questions</h2>
      <details><summary>Is it really free? What's the catch?</summary><p>No catch. SRIVELTECH makes tools for STEM learners and does not earn from Kerfline. There are no paid features to unlock.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need the internet?</summary><p>Only to open the web version the first time. The downloaded file works fully offline.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Where are my drawings saved?</summary><p>In your own browser, on your device. With the downloaded app you can also run the optional folder server, which saves drawings as files in a folder on your computer. Nothing is uploaded anywhere.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I open files from other drawing programs?</summary><p>SVG files open as editable shapes, and pictures open too. For other programs' own file types, export SVG or PDF from that program first.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Will my laser software read the DXF?</summary><p>It is the classic DXF that cutting programs read, in millimetres. Red lines are cut lines in most laser software; check your machine's colour settings once.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Does it work on a phone or Chromebook?</summary><p>Yes, in a modern browser. A mouse or pen is easiest for detailed work.</p></details>
    </section>

    <section class="final" aria-labelledby="final">
      <h2 id="final">Make something today</h2>
      <p class="sub" style="margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto">Free, in your browser, in under a minute.</p>
      <div class="ctas"><a class="btn primary" href="https://kerfline.surge.sh">Open Kerfline</a></div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
